    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a clear focal point in **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, who earns our highest efficiency score of 80.98. Facing a favorable matchup against McGreevy (4.53 xERA) and batting at the top of the order, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** benefits from a massive 14% boost due to dynamic platoon advantages and a 10% premium for his lead-off spot, making him the cornerstone of our lineup. Following closely, **Yordan Alvarez** (66.84) and **Kyle Schwarber** (66.79) provide the necessary high-floor stability; while **Yordan Alvarez** contends with a slight park disadvantage, his elite 0.464 xwOBA keeps his efficiency strong, and **Kyle Schwarber** continues to be a high-upside play given his anticipated lead-off role against Prielipp.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Christian Encarnacion-Strand**, who narrowly missed the cut at 42.91. While he brings an enticing 0.385 xwOBA to the table, the negative pressure from Seymour\u2019s xERA (3.34) and a significant park penalty forced us to favor more efficient matchups like **Dillon Dingler** (63.89), who remains a high-value play today due to a favorable platoon split against Kay. We are also closely monitoring the lineup status of **Trea Turner** and **Gary Sanchez**; while **Trea Turner** offers elite speed upside, his score is slightly tempered by the prospect of facing an elite hold pitcher in Prielipp, while **Gary Sanchez** remains a strong play provided he locks into that #3 spot against Wrobleski.\n\nRisks remain on the periphery, particularly for **Kazuma Okamoto** (42.19) and **Caleb Durbin** (47.15), both of whom are facing challenging arms in Schlittler and Jones. **Kazuma Okamoto** in particular carries a heavy -19% SP skill penalty, forcing him to the bottom of our start-worthy candidates. We have opted to keep **Josh Smith** on the bench, as his sub-optimal batting order position outweighs the dynamic platoon edge he would have otherwise enjoyed. As we navigate these matchups, keep a close eye on the wind conditions favoring our left-handed bats like **Christian Yelich**, though his efficiency is hampered by a significant platoon disadvantage that keeps him in the marginal start tier.",
